From c1170ff9d09080753d9e0092b0054d0055e8974b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yekai pan <pyk@seas.upenn.edu>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 00:18:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 24/24] l2r-local: entry 23-p: drop stack: one function's
 pending boxes join a run of cells

23-n links every pending box of the glue through its header, which costs
instructions where the glue defers one child per freed cell: a balanced
tree 57.08 -> 63.58 instructions per freed cell, a rose tree 52.77 ->
58.54 (cachegrind, the plain Reussir microbenchmark); binary trees are a
benchmark. A link takes a header read, decode and restore at the pop and
an encode and two stores at the deferral, where a run of cells takes a
push and a pop.

Now a box deferred with defer_wide after a box of the same release
function joins the linked run's cells, as a host's cell joins a run (8
bytes while it waits; for a value of one type usually as many as its
height), and the upper 16 bits of its header's second word are set to 0.
Only a change of release links through the header, as before (40-bit
offset; in the high 8 bits, 1 plus the index of the previous box's
function, so they are never 0 in a link). A pop of a linked run's head
reads those bits: 0, the cells' last one is the head now; else the link,
restored. The order is the same: the run is one entry, its boxes popped
last deferred first. Alternating releases (RtAltTreeFree) still take no
memory per pending box.

The table lookup on a change of release goes through a 16-slot cache of
(function, index) pairs, direct-mapped by address, in the zero-initialized
thread-local beside the table and cleared with it, so that many release
functions do not scan the 255 entries at every link.

Instructions per freed cell (base9-shared / 23-n / this patch): balanced
tree 57.08 / 63.58 / 59.08, rose tree 52.77 / 58.54 / 54.55, alternating
pending nodes 66.07 / 74.60 / 74.60; one-sided chains unchanged.
lean2rr, peak RSS at 10^6 levels: RtAltTreeFree 45.7 MB (native 55.1),
RtDeepTreeFree 37.3, RtClosureChainFree 68.2 (native 102.3) and its
compositions 66.1 MB (native 85.9; with 23-n alone 45.9: one type's
pending boxes are cells again). Also measured, not taken: a same-function
link of one 32-bit store (offset in the count, upper bits 0) gave 61.08
and 56.32.

Tests: the differential test's boxes have garbage in the upper half of
their second word for odd numbers (padding), the releases check count and
tag, and the run with wide boxes must use cells; the releases are reified
once (Miri gives every reification its own address).
